# Gatekeep — build and test

## Tool paths (workspace `.tools/`)

JDK and the Android SDK are **not** on global PATH. They live under the **Private workspace root** (`../.tools/` from `Gatekeep/`):

| Tool | Path |
|------|------|
| **JDK 17** | `c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/jdk-17.0.14+7` |
| **Android SDK** | `c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/android-sdk` |

`Gatekeep/local.properties` already points `sdk.dir` at the Android SDK.

Before Gradle, set:

```bash
export JAVA_HOME="c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/jdk-17.0.14+7"
export ANDROID_HOME="c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/android-sdk"
```

From `Gatekeep/`:

```bash
cd Gatekeep
export JAVA_HOME="c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/jdk-17.0.14+7"
export ANDROID_HOME="c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/android-sdk"
./gradlew :core-domain:test :app:assembleDebug
```

APK output: `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk` (arm64-v8a only; see `app/build.gradle.kts` `abiFilters`).

## Requirements

- JDK 17
- Android SDK 35 (installed in `.tools/android-sdk`)

## Notes

- Room schema bumps require an explicit `Migration` in `core-data` — do **not** use `fallbackToDestructiveMigration()` (profiles would be wiped on upgrade).
- Do not assume `java` or `adb` are on PATH; use the paths above or `local.properties`.
